      content: 'Not every "that-clause" is subjunctive. The subjunctive appears after DEMAND/SUGGEST/REQUIRE-type verbs and IMPORTANCE adjectives. But "suggest" and "insist" can also report a FACT, taking the indicative: "She suggested that he WAS lying" (a claim about reality) vs "She suggested that he LEAVE" (a proposal). Learn to spot meaning: proposal/requirement → subjunctive; report of fact → indicative.',
